BT /F2 22 Tf 72 702 Td (Notes on voices) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 666 Td (Lectern uses the voices installed on your computer, so quality depends on your system.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 650 Td (On Windows the natural sounding Microsoft voices are the best choice when they are) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 634 Td (available; on a Mac the Siri and Enhanced voices are excellent; Chrome also offers its) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 618 Td (own online voices which need an internet connection.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 592 Td (Your place is remembered. When you reopen a document Lectern returns to the page you) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 576 Td (were on, and your voice, speed, and pitch settings are kept between sessions. Nothing) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 560 Td (leaves your computer: the file is read in your browser and never uploaded anywhere.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 72 524 Td (Where it falls short) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 504 Td (Scanned PDFs that contain only images have no text to read. Lectern will show the pages) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 488 Td (but the Read aloud panel will tell you there is nothing it can speak. Running those) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 472 Td (files through an OCR tool first solves it. Columns, tables, and footnotes are read in) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 456 Td (the order the PDF stores them, which is usually, but not always, the order you would) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 440 Td (read them in.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 414 Td (That is the whole tour. Close this file, open one of your own, and press play.) Tj ET
